# 🧩 **Harness Initialization Sequence (v1.0)**  
This is the canonical initialization procedure for the tri‑stream harness.

```json
{
  "initialization_sequence": {
    "version": "1.0",
    "phases": [
      {
        "phase": "preflight",
        "actions": [
          "Load Tri-Stream Schema Definition",
          "Load Tri-Stream Routing Logic",
          "Validate schema integrity",
          "Validate routing constraints"
        ],
        "notes": "Ensures the harness has a stable foundation before activation."
      },
      {
        "phase": "channel_binding",
        "actions": [
          "Create ic_stream channel with altitude A6 and membrane 'narrative'",
          "Create dev_stream channel with altitude A6-dev and membrane 'diagnostic'",
          "Create meta_stream channel with altitude A6-meta and membrane 'interpretive'",
          "Seal each channel with write-only-to-self constraints"
        ],
        "notes": "Channels are created empty but fully sealed."
      },
      {
        "phase": "router_activation",
        "actions": [
          "Initialize tri-stream router",
          "Bind routing rules to channels",
          "Enable read/observe permissions",
          "Reject cross-channel write attempts"
        ],
        "notes": "Router enforces membrane boundaries and altitude separation."
      },
      {
        "phase": "envelope_preparation",
        "actions": [
          "Prepare empty tri-stream envelope",
          "Bind altitude and membrane tags",
          "Attach routing constraints",
          "Attach provenance block"
        ],
        "notes": "Envelope is ready to receive payloads."
      },
      {
        "phase": "ready_state",
        "actions": [
          "Mark harness status as 'ready'",
          "Await IC, Dev, and Meta payloads",
          "Begin tri-stream execution cycle"
        ],
        "notes": "Harness is fully operational."
      }
    ],
    "status": "ready"
  }
}
```

